{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>A crown of gold round about</b> — a symbol of a royal crown, for the table signifies wealth and greatness, as people speak of \"a king's table\" — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 25:24). And so indeed the matter is, for this is the secret of the table: the blessing of HaShem, from the time the world existed, did not bring being from nothingness into existence, but the world follows its customary course, as it is written (Genesis 31[Genesis 1:31]), \"And Elohim saw all that He had made, and behold, it was very good.\" But when there exists a root for the thing, the blessing rests upon it and increases it, as Elisha said, \"Tell me, what do you have in the house?\" (II Kings 4:2), and the blessing rested upon the gathered oil and filled all the vessels, and in Elijah's case, \"The jar of meal was not spent, neither did the cruse of oil fail\" (I Kings 17:16). So too the table with the showbread: upon it the blessing rests, and from it satiety comes to all Israel. Therefore they said: every priest who receives an olive's portion eats and is satisfied (Yoma 39b)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Ramban cites Genesis 1:31 but writes the chapter number as ל\"א (31), which would be Genesis 31; the verse quoted is clearly Genesis 1:31, so I have corrected the citation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:16:22.696632223Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}